  "scope": "# Review \u2014 `ea8116b3e778` (`generator.py` 3.0.0)\n\nScope: prototype/tests/notes only; approved production generator SHA-256 `c00ef1d1a1b3a32a8ef8662534bdf0d83798d3825ed2cdd1d6401994e5415ceb` is unchanged.\nGap \u2192 repair: added an episode-fixed `symmetry_mode` prototype (`horizontal`, `vertical`, `half_turn`, canonical `both`) instead of adding nuisance-only sampler variation.\nCanonical default: `both` returns the exact canonical Racket text and normalized SHA-256 `4e2d4d62614f7d987f3046db60dc33c2d6995786fd0d3e1e7bd9e61c6be52c98`.\nTeaching contract: the same lawful `single_quadrant` inputs are reused across settings; each retained demonstration and query separates the selected rule from all three rivals.\nRetained batch: four settings \u00d7 (2 demonstrations + 4 distinct queries), with independent count controls and answer-free public projections.\nExact execution: 24 selected labels and 96 Racket program/pair checks; all Python/Racket comparisons passed, with 24/24 demo-rival and 48/48 query-rival disagreements.\nEvidence: `checks/parametric/ea8116b3e778-symmetry-mode.json`; replay artifacts are under `generators/ea8116b3e778/workspace/parametric/materialized/`.\nTests: final aggregate passed 25/25 in 36.29s (49.88s including wrapper/Racket setup): 16 legacy selected-generator tests plus 9 new parametric tests.\nAdversarial surfaces: parameter/Racket parity; hidden-field-independent public IDs; exact numeric/count boundaries; tamper rejection; duplicate/distinct-input constraints; cleanup preservation and symlink rejection.\nReference-rule changes: none. Generator selection, canonical authority, rule hash, and approval metadata remain unchanged.",
